                  <div class=3D"container">
                    =20
                        <p></p><p>Raquel Buscaino leads Deloitte=E2=80=99s =
Novel &amp; Exponential Technologies (NExT) team, where she and her team un=
cover and shape the emerging technologies most likely to change how we work=
 and live. From brain-computer interfaces and synthetic biology to space ex=
ploration and quantum computing, she helps distill signal from noise, ident=
ify practical value in a sea of hype, and turn ambiguous concepts into stra=
tegic direction.</p>
<p>Through NExT, Buscaino helps shape Deloitte=E2=80=99s global thought lea=
dership, including <a href=3D"https://www.deloitte.com/us/en/insights/topic=
s/technology-management/tech-trends.html"><i>Tech Trends</i></a> and indust=
ry-specific insights; and she brings a clear, market-facing point of view o=
n what=E2=80=99s new, what matters, and what comes next. She is invited reg=
ularly to speak at global technology conferences, and she also previously h=
osted Deloitte=E2=80=99s <a href=3D"https://www.deloitte.com/content/websit=
es/us/en/about/collections/techtalks-podcast-series."><i>TECHTalks podcast<=
/i></a>, where she interviewed industry leaders on the technologies and ide=
as defining the future.</p>
<p>She previously worked in Deloitte=E2=80=99s blockchain and digital asset=
s practice, where she specialized in blockchain consortiums and led global =
workshops for Deloitte and its clients. In addition to her work at Deloitte=
, Buscaino is an adjunct professor at the University of Southern California=
 where she teaches an MBA course on AI.</p>
<p>Across her roles, she brings a combination of strategic insight, technic=
al fluency, and approachable storytelling that helps CxOs make confident de=
cisions in fast-changing markets.</p>
<p></p>
