                  <div class=3D"container">
                    =20
                        <p></p><p>As Deloitte=E2=80=99s US Chief Technology=
 Officer, Bill helps clients anticipate the impact that new and emerging te=
chnologies may have on their organization in the future, while getting ther=
e from the realities of today. In this role, he identifies, researches, and=
 champions the emerging technologies affecting clients=E2=80=99 businesses.=
 Bill also drives the incubation of new assets, solutions, and businesses a=
cross Deloitte=E2=80=99s industries and offerings, while shaping the strate=
gy for Deloitte=E2=80=99s evolving technology-related services, talent mode=
l, and market positioning.&nbsp;</p>
<p>Bill is a principal in Deloitte Consulting LLP. For more than 25 years, =
Bill has delivered complex transformation programs for clients in a variety=
 of industries, including Financial Services, Life Sciences &amp; Health Ca=
re, Consumer, Telecommunications, Energy, and the Public Sector. Bill also =
serves as executive sponsor of Deloitte=E2=80=99s CIO Program, offering CIO=
s and other tech executives insights and experiences to navigate the comple=
x and evolving challenges they face in business and technology. Previously,=
 Bill was the founding global leader of Deloitte Digital where he was respo=
nsible for launching and growing a new global practice, redefining the visi=
on of a digital agency.&nbsp;</p>
<p>Bill earned his undergraduate degree in Computer Engineering from the Un=
iversity of Notre Dame, and his MBA from the Kellogg School of Management a=
t Northwestern University.&nbsp; He proudly serves on the Board of Director=
s for the Kids In Need Foundation - partnering with teachers and students i=
n under-resourced schools, providing the support needed for teachers to tea=
ch and learners to learn.&nbsp; He also chairs the Business Advisory Counci=
l of the Starlight Theater, the largest open-air venue in the Midwest that =
sponsors a variety of programs to expand access and involvement in the arts=
.</p>
<p></p>
